      -- projext-undo mirror manifests; collisions accepted (docs/pextStore.md § Mirror).
  @api util.toBase36(n)  @ 324-333
  @api util.fromBase36(txt)  @ 335-337
  @api util.toBase62(n)  @ 343-352
  @api util.fromBase62(txt)  @ 354-363
  @api util.dotimes(n, v)  @ 366-374
      @contract  overloaded on type of v: function => call n times for side effect; else build n-array filled with v  @ 365
  @api util.serialise(value, exclude, seen)  @ 377-417
      @contract  strict: cycles raise; exclude applies only to the outermost table (recursion drops it)  @ 376
  @api util.unserialise(input)  @ 420-535
      @contract  strict: trailing chars after the root value raise; scalars decode back to number/boolean/string  @ 419
  @api util.prettySerialise(value)  @ 615-617
      @contract  emits a `return <literal>` chunk for load(); non-finite → 1/0 -1/0 0/0; cycles raise  @ 614
  @api util.prettyUnserialise(text)  @ 620-626
      @contract  sandboxed load() of the disk literal (text-only, empty env); ok→value, fail→nil,err  @ 619
  @api util.instantiate(name, deps)  @ 630-636
      @contract  executes the named module file as a fresh chunk, passing `deps` as its `...` argument. Used for factory modules whose file body IS the constructor (vs. stateless `require`d tables). Test seam: a function in util._stubs[name] takes precedence and is called with deps — so harnesses can swap a fake without altering the production graph.  @ 628

